    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 85.94 score, benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against Lowder\u2019s 5.25 xERA and a prime slot in the #2 hole. His capacity for stolen bases remains our primary engine, and today\u2019s matchup allows for maximum exploitation of the basepaths. Following closely are **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.83) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17), both of whom capitalize on high-ceiling platoon advantages and favorable order positioning. **James Wood** also presents a compelling start at 65.46; despite a tougher matchup against Castillo, Wood\u2019s elite 0.403 xwOBA and lead-off spot make him a high-floor asset for today\u2019s offensive output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 44.90 score. While **Riley** possesses significant pop, the combination of Manaea\u2019s 3.43 xERA and a park penalty suppressed his efficiency just enough to keep him behind the more favorable platoon profiles of **Kyle Karros** and **Dalton Rushing**. We are monitoring the risk profile of **Brice Turang** closely; while his 54.45 score is solid, he faces Nola, whose ability to hold runners (57% SB suppression) significantly dampens **Turang**\u2019s stolen base upside. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** remains a start despite a challenging matchup against Gausman, as his aggressive sprint profile is needed to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category, even though his platoon-adjusted score suffered today.",
